// BT-3051: exercises `^self <inheritedSelector>` directly — a self-send fed
// straight to `^` as its own argument, rather than assigned to a local first
// (`result := self foo. ^result`, the workaround BT-3047's own fixtures used
// to sidestep this exact bug). `foo` is inherited from BT3047Ancestor and the
// block executes inside another class's process (ADR 0109), so this also
// exercises the NLR-throw codegen path, not just the plain-return path.

BT3047Ancestor subclass: BT3051Parent

  class returnFooThrough: aDriverClass over: aList :: List -> Symbol =>
    aDriverClass run: [:x | ^self foo] over: aList
    #wrong
